{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:8-6","provision":"BCO 8-6","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"8-6","title":"Section 8-6","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/8-6/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/8-6","current_text":{"html":"<p>When a teaching elder is appointed to the work of an evangelist in foreign countries or where there are no other PCA churches within a reasonable distance, he is commissioned for a renewable term of twelve months to preach the Word, to administer the Sacraments, to receive and dismiss members of mission churches, and to train potential officers. By separate actions the Presbytery may in extraordinary situations commission him to examine, ordain and install ruling elders and deacons and organize churches.</p>","text":"When a teaching elder is appointed to the work of an evangelist in foreign countries or where there are no other PCA churches within a reasonable distance, he is commissioned for a renewable term of twelve months to preach the Word, to administer the Sacraments, to receive and dismiss members of mission churches, and to train potential officers. By separate actions the Presbytery may in extraordinary situations commission him to examine, ordain and install ruling elders and deacons and organize churches."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"f18747b0a32ed7c7de9dcaba7c1efa997c29cabe","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"e860e3cdb8d0e6c1a530fdcee408